ash deficit makes a late surge difficult despite a national environment favorable to Democrats.", "watch": "Fresh independent polling or a stronger-than-expected Democratic midterm wave could narrow a race last measured more than two months ago.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 69 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Mike Haridopolos (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Rep. Mike Haridopolos seeks re-election in this Space Coast district that leaned about eight points Republican at the presidential level. Challenger Jennifer Jenkins, who switched into the race in May, has trailed in the limited polling available. Two July surveys, one Republican-sponsored and one Democratic-sponsored, each showed Haridopolos ahead by nine points, and he led an informed-ballot test at 55 percent.\n\nHaridopolos holds a steep financial advantage, with roughly $1.2 million on hand to Jenkins' $108,000, and has won the U.S. Chamber's endorsement. Most national raters place the race in the Safe or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Jenkins about a 6 percent chance. The main question is whether a favorable national environment for Democrats and local attention to affordability can narrow a race that has drawn little independent polling since midsummer.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0724, "margin": -8.83}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0723, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0928, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0611, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0442, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0553, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0651, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0689, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0604, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0512, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0574, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem":